From 39931ee01f82c71433932cb21daed90094c9446e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Atala <luis.atala@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:13:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] HID: razer-barracuda: query battery, cable and voltage

The headset reports its battery percentage only when it changes, and its
cable state only when the cable is plugged in or out. After the headset
is switched on, both can stay unknown for a long time.

The dongle forwards battery (0x21) and cable (0x2a) GET requests to the
headset only while its diagnostic queries are routed to the headset,
which command E1 selects and E0 reads back. On each confirmed link, after
a cable change and every six minutes while linked:

- check that the headset transport exists (E6 bit 0x08) and that the
  route is local (E0 reads 0);
- select the headset route (E1 01) and verify it;
- send both GETs and a battery voltage query (family 0x06, 0x31);
- restore the local route (E1 00) and verify it.

If the local route cannot be restored after one retry, stop using the
route until the next confirmed link. Sequences are serialized by a mutex
and use their own range of sequence numbers.

Replies to the GETs are decoded like the headset's own reports. A cable
reply after a link is not a cable change, so it does not schedule
another refresh. Expose the voltage as VOLTAGE_NOW. Reading a property
never sends a query.

The GET frame layout comes from a userspace tool for the Barracuda 2.4
(1532:053c).

Link: https://github.com/TarikTopalovic/razer-barracuda-2.4-linux
Assisted-by: LLM sparse
---
 drivers/hid/hid-razer-barracuda-test.c | 130 +++++++++
 drivers/hid/hid-razer-barracuda.c      | 353 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 471 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-razer-barracuda-test.c b/drivers/hid/hid-razer-barracuda-test.c
